# DB Monitor — Semantic Memory Blocks
# Each block is a dense domain map prefixed with space-separated keywords.
# The 9B agent retrieves ONLY the blocks matching user keywords via Goose Memory.
# Do NOT load all blocks at once. Match keywords, load relevant block, act.

================================================================================
#configuration #config #env #environment #settings #postgres #kafka #broker #jwt #webhook #otel #retention #quota #tuning #production #validation
================================================================================

DOMAIN: Configuration & Environment Variables
FILES: src/db_monitor/config.py (thin proxy to core/config_loader.py), src/db_monitor/core/config_loader.py (utility functions), app/config.py (legacy monolith — ~400 lines of env var loading, the actual source of truth for all config constants)
NOTE: app/config.py is NOT a shim — it is the real config module. src/db_monitor/config.py proxies to it. Read app/config.py for the full set of env var loading and validation rules.
ENTRY: Module-level constants loaded at import time from os.environ via dotenv.

CRITICAL CONSTANTS (all are plain module-level vars, NOT class instances):
- POSTGRES_URL — asyncpg DSN, default "postgresql+asyncpg://postgres:postgres@localhost:5437/postgres"
- KAFKA_BROKER — default "kafka:9092"
- KAFKA_TOPICS — CSV list, auto-derived from connectors/sources.json manifest when env var absent
- BROKER_CLUSTERS — JSON array of {name, broker_kind, bootstrap_servers, topics, consumer_group, ...}
- KAFKA_CLUSTERS — legacy single-kind format, superseded by BROKER_CLUSTERS
- MESSAGE_BROKER — "kafka" or "rabbitmq", selects default cluster builder
- JWT_SECRET / JWT_SECRET_NEXT — HS256 signing, rotation support
- JWT_ALGORITHM — default "HS256"
- ACCESS_TOKEN_TTL_MINUTES — default 15
- WS_SESSION_TOKEN_TTL_SECONDS — default 60
- DB_POOL_SIZE / DB_MAX_OVERFLOW / DB_POOL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS — asyncpg pool tuning
- DB_SCHEMA_MODE — "apply" | "validate" | "skip", controls startup migration behavior
- APP_ENV — "development" | "production", production enforces stricter validation
- ALLOW_BOOTSTRAP — disabled in production, enables POST /auth/bootstrap
- DLQ_ENABLED / BATCH_ENABLED / BATCH_SIZE — consumer behavior toggles
- RETENTION_CLEANUP_ENABLED / RETENTION_CLEANUP_INTERVAL_SECONDS — background cleanup
- EVENT_RETENTION_DAYS / COLUMN_CHANGES_RETENTION_DAYS / DEAD_LETTER_RETENTION_DAYS / API_AUDIT_LOG_RETENTION_DAYS
- INGESTION_QUOTA_ENABLED / INGESTION_QUOTA_WINDOW_SECONDS / INGESTION_QUOTA_MODE ("throttle"|"drop")
- WEBHOOK_URLS / WEBHOOK_SHARED_SECRET / WEBHOOK_TIMEOUT_SECONDS / WEBHOOK_MAX_RETRIES
- OTEL_TRACING_ENABLED / OTEL_SERVICE_NAME / OTEL_EXPORTER ("otlp"|"console")
- AUDIT_LOG_QUEUE_MAXSIZE / AUDIT_LOG_BATCH_SIZE / AUDIT_LOG_FLUSH_INTERVAL_SECONDS
- APP_SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT_SECONDS — default 45
- READINESS_MAX_COMMIT_AGE_SECONDS / READINESS_MAX_CONSUMER_LAG / READINESS_MAX_DLQ_MESSAGES
- SLO_ROLLING_WINDOW_DAYS / TENANT_COHORT_SLO_POLICIES — JSON array of cohort SLO tiers
- WS_BACKPLANE_ENABLED / WS_BACKPLANE_CHANNEL — Postgres LISTEN/NOTIFY clustering

PRODUCTION VALIDATION RULES (APP_ENV=production):
- DB_POOL_SIZE >= 1, DB_MAX_OVERFLOW >= 0, DB_POOL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS >= 1
- POSTGRES_URL must NOT be the default localhost URL
- JWT_SECRET must be explicitly set and >= 32 chars
- OTEL_EXPORTER must be "otlp" or "console"; if otlp, endpoint required
- MESSAGE_BROKER must be "kafka" or "rabbitmq"
- All *_DAYS retention values must be >= 0
- WEBHOOK_URLS entries must start with http:// or https://

HELPER FUNCTIONS (in core/config_loader.py):
- get_env_or_file(env_name, default) — reads env var or file path (for secrets)
- parse_csv_list(value) — splits comma-separated strings
- config_error(message, hint) — raises ValueError with remediation hint

PITFALLS:
- Config is loaded at IMPORT TIME. Changing env vars after import has no effect.
- BROKER_CLUSTERS and KAFKA_CLUSTERS are mutually exclusive config paths.
- JWT_SECRET_NEXT enables zero-downtime rotation; both secrets are tried during decode.

